WEBVTT

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:07.400
<i>Um, I have to give my periodic report
to the headmaster</i>

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.320
<i>and make a text
for Furuhashi and Ogata today.</i>

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.780
Nariyuki!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:12.780
Take that!

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:15.110
Let me borrow your notebook!

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.200
Hey, stop doing that
whenever you see me,

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.200
Uruka Takemoto!

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:25.960
My bad, my bad!
I'm on my way to practice!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.840
So, I won't have time to do
the homework that's due tomorrow.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.010
But yours is already done, right?

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.130
So, let me borrow it! Let me copy it!
Just give it to me!

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:38.640
We went to the same middle school,
but you can't do stuff like this.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.930
You need to do your own homework
once in a while.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.600
Please show it to me!

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.020
I hate studying!

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.020
That guy!

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:19.200
HEADMASTER

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.830
That's all I have for this report.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:26.330
EPISODE 2:
A FISH IS TO WATER
AS A GENIUS IS TO X

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.210
To sum up, Ogata and Furuhashi
have begun to improve little by little.

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.710
I see. Thank you for the report.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.300
By the way, Yuiga...

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:38.970
I hear you've been friends
with Uruka Takemoto since middle school.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.970
Yes. What about it?

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:46.270
As a sports scholarship student,
she really has extraordinary athletic skills,

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:49.310
and as the star of the swim team
and pride of this academy,

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:52.270
she snatches victory
with her freestyle everywhere.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:55.610
They call her the "Shimmering
Ebony Mermaid Princess."

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.820
However, her schoolwork is a disaster.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:00.490
<i>I'm a dumbbell! Yum!</i>

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.830
She hopes to have a recommendation,
but that's up in the air.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.200
By the way, Yuiga,

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:11.920
there's one more girl I'd like you to tutor.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.000
<i>There's no way.</i>

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:18.090
THERE'S NO WAY

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.630
<i>I only wish I could've told him that.</i>

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.090
<i>But not when the special
VIP recommendation is on the line.</i>

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.810
<i>She was amazing back in middle school,</i>

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.060
<i>but she's even faster now.</i>

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.650
<i>She's not a future Olympics contender
for nothing.</i>

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.730
Huh? Nariyuki!

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.070
What, are you here to peep at me?

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.780
What a lecher!

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.030
Wrong! And you don't have to pose!

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:47.280
I need to talk to you.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:52.000
You, be my tutor?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.710
With the sports recommendation,
you can go to Otowa University, right?

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.550
How do you know about that?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.300
With a sports recommendation,
I don't have to study!

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.180
This year, they want
"well-rounded students,"

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.180
with not only results from meets,
but also test results, now including English.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:12.980
Then, I won't go there!

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.810
Is your life that lightweight?

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:18.770
Sorry, but my special
VIP recommendation is on the line.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.070
So, like it or not, you're gonna study!

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.610
I don't wanna study!

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.030
Get back here! Do as I say!

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.660
Forget it!

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.870
Hey, get back here! For crying out loud!

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.160
No way!

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.290
Nariyuki!

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:39.960
Th-Thanks...

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:43.970
Look, Nariyuki, if you can't swim,
don't run by the pool.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.300
Incidentally, Takemoto...

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.390
Gotcha!

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:51.220
That's low!

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.100
There he is! Yuiga,
the headmaster said you were here.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.360
No! Get off of me!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.570
Struggle all you like, I've got you now!

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:04.070
I'm going to teach you a lesson all right!

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.160
Yuiga, no!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.660
Ow! What the hell
are you doing, Furuhashi?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.450
Th-Th-Th-Th-That's my line!

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:12.830
Scumbag.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.250
Like you're looking at filth?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.580
I think you two have the wrong idea!

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:21.090
Not really. I couldn't care
one picometer about this.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:25.300
Huh? The two geniuses of our school!
You know them, Nariyuki?

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:27.760
Um...

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.010
Actually...

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:31.010
I see.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:34.270
So, even geniuses have
a weak point, huh?

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:39.150
Yuiga has been a big help, though,
tutoring us with all he's got.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.570
Then, we're in the same boat!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.700
Because starting today,
Nariyuki's gonna be my tutor, too!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:50.830
We'll be together!

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:54.200
Um, you're splashing.
I mean, you're too close for comfort.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:57.540
Takemoto, why are you so enthusiastic

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.790
when you were so unwilling
just a minute ago?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.170
Oh, what's the difference?
That's water under the bridge.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:08.130
<i>What the hell? Why? The second
Furuhashi and Ogata got here...</i>

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:09.390
<i>I don't get it.</i>

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:14.100
<i>Well, in any case, it worked out,
so I guess I'll let it go.</i>

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:24.020
NARIYUKI YUIGA

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.020
<i>Hey, Yuiga!</i>

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.360
<i>Let me borrow your notebook!</i>

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.030
<i>Again? You're incorrigible!</i>

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:29.700
<i>Don't copy it verbatim!</i>

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.820
<i>Yay!</i>

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:36.040
<i>Yuiga always lets me see his homework.
He's convenient to have around.</i>

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.170
<i>Now that I'm done copying it,
I'll just give it back to him.</i>

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.500
<i>Hey, Nari...</i>

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:44.880
<i>Why do you always let Takemoto
copy your notebook?</i>

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.420
<i>There's nothing in it for you.</i>

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:51.390
<i>Well, it's not like I'd just
show it to anyone,</i>

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:55.140
<i>but I know she's sacrificed a lot,
including studying and having fun,</i>

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.930
<i>so she can go all out with swimming.</i>

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.600
<i>That's what you say,
but I bet you like her!</i>

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.230
<i>Those tan lines are sexy, right?</i>

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:05.650
<i>Dumbass! It's not like that!</i>

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:12.530
<i>I know that Nariyuki does
his very best for everybody.</i>

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.450
<i>But then,</i>

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:19.160
<i>at least, I'll make him
work the hardest for me!</i>

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:25.960
<i>"Can I borrow your notebook?"
"Can you lend me your notebook?"
Okay, act normal, act normal...</i>

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:27.550
Ogata!

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.550
Yes?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:30.220
What is it, sir?

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.930
Don't give me "What is it?"

00:07:32.180 --> 00:07:34.800
You're the only one
who hasn't turned in the assignment.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.760
But that's...

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:40.140
I'll give you until tomorrow,
so turn it in by then. Got it?

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.190
I'm doomed.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:49.070
So, I came here again at night
like you asked, Ogata,

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.400
and you want me to tell you
the trick to writing a short essay?

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:57.620
Yes. I'll be in hot water
if I don't turn it in by tomorrow.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.910
You know, this udon is really good.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.660
We're proud of it.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.580
Please help me when you're done.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.420
<i>This is bribery!</i>

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:09.210
<i>With my family out
at a gathering of relatives tonight,</i>

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.880
<i>I'd planned on focusing
on my own studies for once, but...</i>

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:17.720
"About the connection
between civilization and people."

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.520
I've tried turning it in
several times before,

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:22.890
but the teacher rejected it each time.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:26.520
I'm not really interested.
So, I've got nothing.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.520
There's got to be a little more than this.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.360
Not that I could think of.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:32.490
It's impossible for me to write
about something that doesn't have a solution.

00:08:32.740 --> 00:08:37.320
Still, all I can do is teach you
the fundamentals.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:41.250
GOOD EVENING, SMOOCHIES!

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:44.290
<i>Good evening, smoochies! I don't have
practice tonight, so I'm singing karaoke!</i>

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:45.960
<i>Come on over, Rizzy!</i>

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:50.210
<i>Fumino already turned me down
because she's studying!</i>

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.710
<i>Love you!</i>

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:55.930
<i>Wow, she must really be looking
at something nasty.</i>

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.760
I'm not going.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.600
I'm studying at Yuiga's house right now.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.110
Rizzy, what a coincidence!

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:11.780
Takemoto!

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:16.490
Actually, I just thought of something
I wanted Nariyuki to teach me, too!

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.450
I thought you were doing karaoke.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.780
Squish!

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:25.660
OGATA UDON

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.990
Wh-Wh-Wh-What was that?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:23.790
Rizzy, you've got big boobs,

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.660
so cut me some slack!

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:30.380
Huh? I don't have anything to write with.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:32.340
You don't intend to study at all, do you?

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.680
Jeez. Fine, I'll lend you
the textbook. Wait here.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.350
That was a surprise!

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.310
A blackout? Or a breaker?

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.520
That's strange.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.430
I'm sure we paid
our electric bill this month.

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:49.020
This is your first guess.
That's so you Nariyuki.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:50.400
Check it!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:54.150
All the street lights are out, too!

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:56.400
Then it's definitely a power outage.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:10:00.320
Yay! It's exciting when there's a blackout!

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.620
Why?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.870
It's beyond my comprehension.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.830
Why are you in such high spirits
over a power outage?

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.170
Um, Ogata...

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.880
- Do you have a fear of the dark—
- Not even one picometer's worth.

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.180
Huh? My phone died.

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:30.100
<i>Ogata, Ogata...</i>

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.190
<i>You're totally scared
of the dark, aren't you?</i>

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.860
<i>Huh? I can't see well in the dark,</i>

00:10:38.110 --> 00:10:39.950
<i>but is Rizzy clinging to him?</i>

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.910
<i>Nah. Rizzy would be
the last person to use the dark</i>

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.490
<i>as an opportunity
to snuggle up with someone.</i>

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.870
<i>Wait, I could do that!</i>

00:10:49.870 --> 00:10:51.750
<i>Nariyuki, I'm scared!</i>

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.920
<i>That's cute, Uruka.</i>

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:55.880
<i>A-All right, here I go!</i>

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.510
<i>I'll jump into his arms!</i>

00:10:57.510 --> 00:10:59.430
<i>Now's your chance, Uruka Takemoto!</i>

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.010
O-Oh no. Nariyuki, I'm scared.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:06.600
What's wrong, Takemoto?

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.310
<i>I can't!</i>

00:11:08.310 --> 00:11:11.940
<i>If I had that kind of courage, I would've
confessed my feelings to him in middle school!</i>

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:15.150
<i>Wh-What's going on here?</i>

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.070
<i>Ogata, I can understand,
but Takemoto being afraid of the dark?</i>

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:23.240
Takemoto, Ogata, don't worry.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.990
ALUMINUM FOIL

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.990
SALAD OIL

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.290
A makeshift candle!

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:34.170
With salad oil, tissues and aluminum foil,
anyone can make one in no time.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.170
We're used to the power going out here.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:40.970
On nights like that,
I use illumination like this to study by.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.720
Nariyuki, I can't really join you
in laughing about that.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.850
It reminds me of a birthday.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.270
Yeah, right?

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:54.270
No, that was a verbal slip.
Please forget I said anything.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.150
As for me,

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.820
electricity is convenient,
and it's a pain when I can't use it,

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:04.740
but I don't mind sitting in the dark
with a candle like this once in a while.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.620
It feels like the distance between people
really narrows at a time like this.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:20.130
Well, maybe there is
that aspect to it.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:26.100
By the way,
how long will this candle last?

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:29.180
With that amount of oil,
probably about half an hour.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:30.310
Seriously?

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:32.480
It went out!

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.810
Because you blew on it!

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.270
What should we do, Nariyuki?

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.020
FLAIL FLAIL

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.060
Hey, calm down, Takemoto!

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:40.030
Um, the lighter should be around here.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:40.780
THUD

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.990
Hey, Yuiga, that's—

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:45.240
H-Huh? That wasn't it?
I mean, who said that?

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.240
Wh-Where are you touching me, Nariyuki?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:53.080
Looks like the power's back on.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:58.920
Huh? What's the matter, you two?

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:02.300
Wait a second! What? What is it?

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.670
Scumbag!

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:05.970
Yikes! What the heck did I do?

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.680
I'M A PERVERT

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:11.770
U-Um...

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:13.730
Well, now that the power is back on,

00:13:13.980 --> 00:13:17.650
why don't we continue with your essay?

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:18.560
No.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.690
Never mind. I'm going home.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.320
Wait! We can still do it!

00:13:24.320 --> 00:13:25.610
Well, goodbye.

00:13:25.610 --> 00:13:27.110
Ogata!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:33.000
You wrote the essay?

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:37.040
Yes. When I turned it in,
the teacher finally accepted it.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.830
Then, what was last night about?

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.880
It's because of you, Yuiga.

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.300
Thank you.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.380
S-S-Sure.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.850
Is that Ogata's short essay?

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.930
Yes. She finally turned in a proper essay.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.810
"When we're away
from the protection of civilization,

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:04.110
perhaps we become able to see the proper
distance between people in a new light."

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:07.530
Banal. In fact,
that's an immature point of view.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:11.240
You're as harsh as always, Ms. Kirisu.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:15.870
But you have to remember
Ogata is the one who wrote this opinion.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.960
I would call that progress.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:27.340
<i>It seems the latest tutor has had
just a bit of success with Ogata.</i>

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.300
<i>But...</i>

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.260
DAY AND TIME: 4/25, 3 PM
SECTION: ENGLISH BOOK, PAGES 20-40

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.260
REGARDING THE SPECIAL SPORTS CLASS'
ENGLISH VOCABULARY TEST

00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:35.930
FAILING WILL RESULT IN SUPPLEMENTARY LESSONS.
(AND NO CLUB ACTIVITIES.)

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.520
H-Help me, Nariyuki!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.770
50 words by next week
or you'll have to take more lessons?

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.610
Yeah! And if I take supplementary lessons,
I can't do club activities!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.030
What should I do?

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:49.950
Why not memorize them?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.120
As if it's got nothing to do with you!

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.910
How about showing a little more love?

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:57.830
It has 0% to do with him,
and there is no love involved.

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.040
What else can I say but "memorize them"?

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.000
Oh, you don't understand!

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.960
You don't know how hard
it is for me to remember things!

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:07.670
Don't sound like you're proud of that.

00:15:09.590 --> 00:15:11.140
All right, fine.

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.970
You know what the words on the test
are going to be, right?

00:15:14.220 --> 00:15:15.890
Why don't we try testing you now?

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.100
Yum, yum!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:28.570
ENGLISH VOCABULARY
25 QUESTION TEST
NAME: URUKA TAKEMOTO

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:20.140
It's too bad about your swim team.

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:21.940
Well, we're going to take off.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.560
Don't rush to judgment!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:27.400
How many of the vocabulary words
do you know, Rizzy?

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:28.570
Me?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:31.530
This is the quiz I took today.

00:15:32.490 --> 00:15:33.990
68?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:37.580
H-How? I was so confident!

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:40.870
Not just vocabulary words.
I got average on my English tests.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:44.210
I know! Fumino,
we're on the same side, right?

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:50.510
But I'm just pretty good at memorization.

00:15:50.510 --> 00:15:53.510
On regular English tests,
I just score about average, too.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.890
Look, anyone can memorize.

00:15:56.890 --> 00:15:58.640
<i>Furuhashi, stop already!</i>

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:00.680
Listen, Takemoto!

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:03.480
All you need is patience for memorization.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:06.400
You write the words over and over
until you remember them.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.980
You can ignore antonyms
and derivatives.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.320
First, master one word, one meaning.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.490
Then, say the word
and its meaning over and over

00:16:14.740 --> 00:16:16.780
until the sound of it sticks in your ear.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:21.040
Pay attention to the phonetic symbol
and keep the correct pronunciation in mind!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:26.170
WORN-OUT

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:26.170
Don't make a face
like you're about to puke.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:27.920
Oof.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:30.710
All right, Uruka, let's do our best!

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:33.470
Okay? We'll help you, too!

00:16:33.470 --> 00:16:34.130
We?

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.100
Great, thanks, Fumino!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:41.180
<i>I-Is it just me or when I look at her
from this distance,</i>

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:43.020
<i>is Fumino a stunning beauty?</i>

00:16:43.350 --> 00:16:46.980
<i>Silky hair, beautiful skin, long eyelashes...</i>

00:16:47.230 --> 00:16:50.860
<i>On top of that, she's so kind
that it makes me want to protect her.</i>

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.240
<i>And she smells wonderful!</i>

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:56.070
<i>Frankly, she's my ideal!</i>

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:00.240
<i>Does Nariyuki also like a girl like this?</i>

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.120
<i>I'm sure he does.</i>

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:05.370
<i>I can't compete against Fumino
on anything.</i>

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:09.090
<i>There is one thing!</i>

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:10.960
Hey, Takemoto!

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.550
I haven't seen you do any writing.

00:17:13.880 --> 00:17:16.090
All right! I'm not gonna lose!

00:17:16.090 --> 00:17:19.260
Whether it's memorization
or whatever, come and get me!

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:21.390
Huh? I wonder why that is...

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:23.980
I feel like I just took
mysterious emotional damage.

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:25.980
JOMATHAN'S

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.440
Enough already.

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:34.530
I'm sick of studying!

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.030
I want to swim!

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:40.240
Takemoto, please stop
saying that every five minutes.

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.750
Don't you have
any power of concentration?

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:49.040
It's okay, it's okay, Uruka.
Try to hang in there a little longer.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.050
Something's come out of Furuhashi!

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.340
Get back in there!

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:57.590
This is so hard!
Studying isn't fun at all!

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.470
Oh, listen, I was thinking,

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:05.350
with this kind of thing, maybe you can
first show me how much fun English is.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.190
It isn't fun.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.770
For someone who can't do it,
of course studying is tough.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:14.860
As long as they can't do it,
it can never become fun.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:20.660
But if you start there, then laboriously
accumulate a little at a time,

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.490
I think you'll have fun with it
for the first time.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.080
Even for you, Takemoto.

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:28.710
It's not like you loved swimming
from the very beginning, right?

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.630
R-Right.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.420
<i>Dammit!</i>

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:36.550
At first, I just practiced single-mindedly
every day, driven by frustration.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:39.470
True, swimming didn't actually become fun

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:43.010
until I started
breaking my previous records.

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.890
Wh-What? You remember that?

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:48.980
That's creepy, Nariyuki.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:49.770
<i>I'm so happy!</i>

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:53.900
Well, when it comes to swimming,
your ability to focus is second to none.

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:56.650
I often thought I could learn from you.

00:18:58.200 --> 00:18:59.820
Th-That's it!

00:19:03.950 --> 00:19:05.450
Let's go, Takemoto!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.660
"Degree"!

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:18.260
AMOUNT

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:19.760
Amount!

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:20.760
Correct!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:22.430
Next, "essential"!

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.310
INDISPENSABLE

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.480
Indispensable!

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:29.350
"Coast"!

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:34.020
Beach!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.190
- "Estimate"!
- Roughly calculate!

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.650
- "Climate"!
- Weather conditions!

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.610
"Pupil"!

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:39.700
Student!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.320
50 out of 50!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.120
Thanks, you guys!

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:46.290
Yes!

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:47.620
Yay!

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:50.460
My hypothesis that Takemoto's
ability to focus with swimming

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:52.000
could be applied to studying.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.250
I'm proud of you, Yuiga!

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.210
Jeez, why did I have to get roped into this?

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:58.960
This took time
away from my own studies—

00:19:59.300 --> 00:20:00.930
Thank you, too, Rizzy!

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.220
Wh-What are you doing?

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:07.220
What? Well, we're at the pool
wearing swimsuits, so we have to swim!

00:20:07.220 --> 00:20:07.970
Good point!

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.430
Oh no, not me.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:13.650
Huh? Rizzy, can you not swim either?

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:16.270
That's offensive.

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:19.360
Please refrain
from belittling me, Takemoto.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:22.990
Oh no, Ri!

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:26.990
Rizzy acts tough even when she's got
nothing to back it up.

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:28.870
She swims at my level!

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:33.370
All right!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:35.460
The test should be a breeze now.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.420
I can swim as free as a fish!

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:38.460
Listen,

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:40.710
even though you remember it now,

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:42.380
you'd better keep at it
so you don't forget right away.

00:20:42.630 --> 00:20:45.220
Keep reviewing until the test.

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:47.430
Hey, Nariyuki...

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:50.850
You said before that studying is tough.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:52.270
Yeah.

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:56.400
I agree with you, and I hate studying.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:01.190
But even when it's tough,
working hard towards a goal

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:04.860
together with my fellow tutees
Fumino and Rizzy has been pretty fun.

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.410
Takemoto...

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:15.290
W-Well, really, the best part has been...
being with you, Nariyuki... Um...

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.130
What about me?

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:20.420
Nothing!

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:28.600
To show my thanks! For today, but also
for all the times you've helped me!

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:30.810
Make sure you use it!

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:32.770
Gotcha!

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:39.610
<i>Maybe being a tutor isn't so bad.</i>

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:15.700
Takemoto...

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:20.920
How am I supposed to use this?
For what?

00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:25.800
I gave Nariyuki the wrong bag!

00:23:22.590 --> 00:23:31.050
PENCIL CASE
SHE MEANT TO GIVE HIM

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:30.630
What kind of girl gives the boy
she likes her own used swimsuit?

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:35.010
Somebody, kill me!

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.180
<i>Next episode,</i>

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.020
NEXT EPISODE:
A GENIUS RESONATES
EMOTIONALLY WITH X

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:40.020
<i>"A Genius Resonates Emotionally with X."</i>
